reading:
Desk is a near-tie for the field's lead. x14a-desk-cross, Desk Terminal, Patched, scored 7.95: second in heat a, in 7 top fours, and first in the soul, style, system and interaction lenses. The judges love four things. (1) The cased terminal is the strongest "the machine speaks here" device in the main camp: thin glass, the title on the glass with one white-hot word and a single block cursor, and the warm-up from a bright line. (2) The patch lead from the case's socket into Coming up's NOW lamp, called the best graft in heat a (style, system, interaction). Machine and desk read as one drawing. (3) Each tube draws its own page's data: the Plans countdown dial with lit day numerals ("a proper 1980s instrument"), the Ideas map, the To do late bars and the Status needle. (4) Rails whose stops are their controls, and 0 small targets.

Four things sank it or held it back:
- **The ring-as-tick on To do.** It is the tour's old failed reach, taken in its uncorrected form. Usability, the skeptic and interaction all asked for the square box back, with the ring kept only as a lamp. Usability gave 7.3 for this alone.
- **The lower left of Home.** The kids' wishes stub leaves a 130px hole (system, style, skeptic, interaction), and Home's lower half has no lamp at all (soul).
- **A desk that is almost colourless** (feedback, style, crossing lessons). On top of that, restaurants still wear amber, which is the late colour.
- **Small faults:**
  - the steel-blue latched slab reads cold (skeptic);
  - Tab reaches the glass's links before the box (interaction);
  - the textarea's focus ring is faint;
  - the downtown blips on the Ideas map collide (soul, system);
  - the Ready lip on Settings is a second header (soul, system);
  - the bar has no Home key (usability);
  - on the phone, "Send where I am" sits on its own row;
  - the Coming up day numerals are not tabular, and the "VERA · FRI 2 OCT" and FROM caps are tracked (type);
  - the plain month grid does not share the dial's numeral (system);
  - the case is still a heavy slab at its lower half (feedback).

The crossing lessons point to what would make it win:
- Close the failed reaches the judges already named. Take the corrected forms (the square tick).
- Fill empty ground with content, never by stretching.
- Give every section exactly one lamp, so the phosphor is back where it reports something.
- Put grounded colour back with named replacements.
- Keep the signature (the case, the glass title and the patch lead) so the line stays distinct in a field the judges called near-identical.
- The title: seven lines share "Give Vera something to plan." This line has one brief, so it must try an untried title. Keep the on-glass setting the soul lens rated best.
